  "seoTitle": "Gunung Dukono and Gunung Ibu Volcanic Activity",
  "metaDescription": "Multiple volcanic events are reported in North Maluku as Gunung Dukono releases ash plumes reaching 1,000 meters and Gunung Ibu records a recent eruption.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Gunung Dukono in North Halmahera released volcanic ash reaching 1,000 meters above its crater.",
    "Gunung Ibu in West Halmahera recorded an eruption on November 27, though no ash column height was observed.",
    "Authorities have maintained alertness levels in response to the recent volcanic activity across the North Maluku region."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The North Maluku province in Indonesia is currently experiencing heightened geological instability with activity reported at multiple sites. Gunung Dukono, located in the North Halmahera Regency, has produced repeated ash emissions, with recent reports indicating plumes rising approximately 1,000 meters above the summit. Simultaneously, Gunung Ibu in the West Halmahera Regency erupted on the morning of November 27, 2026. While official status remains at a cautionary level, the specific height of the ash column from the Gunung Ibu eruption was not visible to observers. These events are part of a broader period of activity in the Indonesian archipelago, following recent reports of eruptions at other sites including Gunung Semeru and Gunung Karangetang. Local agencies continue to monitor these volcanoes and have issued advisories to nearby populations to remain alert due to potential hazards associated with volcanic discharge.",
